      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Annotate a quad, warp by homography\n\n'CV Annotate Points' is a manual point source: RUN THE WORKFLOW ONCE to load the photo into the node, then LEFT-CLICK the preview to add a corner (drag to fine-tune), SHIFT+CLICK to remove. The coordinates live in the node's 'points' field as normalized JSON (saved with the workflow, hand-editable), and come out as a regular point array - the same kind every point utility consumes.\n\n'CV Quad Warp' applies the homography defined by the 4 annotated corners, in any click order (it sorts them TL/TR/BR/BL): 'extract' rectifies the quad into an aspect-preserving rectangle (a manual document scan), 'fill' warps another image INTO the quad on the photo (poster / billboard / screen replacement). Its matrix output is the exact 3x3 homography used - feed it to 'CV Homography Map' to combine the perspective with lens/wave distortions in a single remap pass.\n\nFailure tolerance: with anything other than exactly 4 points, Quad Warp passes the image through with success=false (inspect it below) - the annotation overlay and 'CV Draw Points' still show whatever points exist."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
